        "summary": "χmT for 1 is 55.1 cm3 K mol−1 near room temperature, close to four uncoupled Dy(III) ions (56.6 cm3 K mol−1), and falls to 26.4 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.0 K. Magnetization reaches 21.5 NμB at 2.0 K and 7 T without saturation; M versus H/T curves are nonsuperimposable, indicating anisotropy and/or low-lying excited states. No ac peaks are observed down to 1.8 K, so slow magnetic relaxation is not displayed.",
