      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "Solid-state excitation of 2 at room temperature shows a ligand-centered maximum near 351 nm. Excitation at 351 nm gives Tb(III) f–f emission at 489, 543, 585, and 622 nm (5D4 → 7FJ, J = 6–3). H2MebptpO acts as an antenna. The intensity-weighted average lifetime for 5D4 → 7F5 is about 605 μs; the decay needs at least three exponentials (χ2 < 1.05).",
